  "size_scale_reference": "main_archivo_black",
  "size_scale_method": "OS/2 sCapHeight / unitsPerEm, cross-checked against the 'H' outline; size_scale = ref_cap_em / font_cap_em so all fonts share the reference cap height at the same CSS px.",
  "turkish_notes": [
    "Always set lang=\"tr\" on caption elements (or pass language='tr' to the shaper) so fonts with a TRK locl feature use Turkish forms.",
    "Do NOT use Python str.upper()/lower() for Turkish: 'i'.upper() -> 'I' (should be 'İ'), 'I'.lower() -> 'i' (should be 'ı'), 'İ'.lower() -> 'i' + U+0307 (combining dot, renders as a double dot in some fonts). Use locale-aware casing: i->İ, ı->I before upper(); İ->i, I->ı before lower(). CSS text-transform: uppercase is locale-aware only when lang=\"tr\" is set.",
    "fi ligatures: checked every font; the i-dot stays visible in all of them (separate contour or joined to the f terminal), so 'fiyat' vs 'fıstık' stays distinct. JetBrains Mono has no fi ligature.",
    "Each face is registered as its own family: declare @font-face with exactly the weight/style given here and set font-synthesis: none to avoid faux bold/italic (Archivo Black and Anton are 400 by metadata although visually heavy).",
    "Turkish lira sign ₺ (U+20BA) is missing in main_archivo_black, serif_instrument_italic and mono_jetbrains_xbold (see has_lira_sign); write 'TL' or fall back to another font for ₺."
